        {
            "id": "d13b1dd9-e287-49fb-8ac2-f434b6bcd4d9",
            "build_id": "7ad3d88b-be88-4103-abec-9caba1319c15",
            "round_number": 3,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-28T21:15:02.964751+00:00",
            "notes": "Get [Impact Burst](item_01fa37d8-4355-4ec2-a9af-59bf030e2882) round 3. Way more damage on enemies grouped up on a capture point or payload. The explosion damage also triggers [Chimera's Maw](item_ff7fe205-3c9a-4a44-9d1f-01788c279ffc)'s cooldown reduction. \n\nAs for items, grab [Chimera's Maw](item_ff7fe205-3c9a-4a44-9d1f-01788c279ffc). Synergizes really well with impact burst, especially if you can find a thin chokepoint or sightline to hit multiple enemies with (ie. around a payload or entry to control point at the start of a round). The explosions trigger tons of cooldown reduction and damage even with relatively low AP.\n\nAlso: If debuffs are causing issues, either slows, burn damage, heal reduction, get cushioned padding and keep it until the end of the game. This item can be extremely underrated and I wish there was a purple equivalent with slightly better stats sometimes.\nIf they don't have any of these 3 heroes go for some ability lifesteal with [Energized Bracers](item_f83a1d9e-91f8-4d2c-bd62-c673b8d9fd2e).\n\nAlso also: If they have an extremely annoying Lucio and/or Brig ruining your day with knockbacks, get [Ironclad Cleats](item_afb5c28e-3980-4a7d-85be-785c32217c28) and keep it until late game (round 6)",
